Memory Operating System (MOS)
API Specification v0.1
Abstract

The MOS API Specification defines the standard interface through which agents, applications, workers, and external systems interact with the Memory Operating System.

The API provides access to:

memory creation,
memory retrieval,
learning,
reasoning context,
planning,
reflection,
knowledge management,
execution tracking,
cognitive state.

The MOS API abstracts storage implementation details and provides a stable cognitive interface independent of backend technology.

Chapter 1
API Philosophy

MOS APIs are not database APIs.

They do not expose:

tables,
rows,
SQL queries,
storage locations.

Instead they expose cognitive operations.

The API operates on concepts:

remember,
recall,
learn,
reflect,
plan,
reason,
activate,
evaluate.
