Chapter 6
Core Memory API

The fundamental operations:

remember()

recall()

forget()

update()

consolidate()
remember()

Creates new cognitive information.

Example:

POST /memory/remember

Request:

{
"type":"fact",

"content":{
 "subject":"User",
 "predicate":"likes",
 "object":"Rust"
},

"source":{
 "type":"conversation",
 "id":"session-123"
},

"confidence":0.95
}

Response:

{
"memory_id":"uuid",

"status":"created",

"confidence":0.95,

"provenance":"uuid"
}
recall()

Retrieves relevant cognition.

Example:

POST /memory/recall

Request:

{
"query":
"How does the user prefer coding?",

"context":{
 "task":"software development"
},

"limit":20
}

Response:

{
"memories":[
 {
  "content":"Prefers Rust",
  "confidence":0.94,
  "source":"conversation"
 }
]
}
