Important architectural insight from this specification

The API reveals something fundamental:

MOS is not a "memory database".

It is closer to a cognitive operating system kernel.

The API is analogous to system calls:

Operating System:

open()
read()
write()
fork()
execute()

MOS:

remember()
recall()
learn()
reflect()
plan()
execute()

Applications do not manage memory directly.

They request cognitive services.
